# Mobile screen layout consistency

Tab roots and stack screens share one top chrome and one page-body gutter. Do not invent a
per-screen inset under the title bar.

## Top chrome

- Use **`HeaderBar`** for the slot under the status bar: safe-area inset and a 44pt row. No
  divider, hairline, or shadow under the title.
- Stack titles go through **`ThemedStackHeader`** (already wraps `HeaderBar`).
- Tab roots use the same title slot (Home, Search, …). Page controls such as Home's media-type
  pills and Search's field and chips sit in the body under that bar, not inside it.

## Page body under the bar

The first content below `HeaderBar` uses **`screenBodyInsets(tokens.spacing)`** from
`apps/mobile/src/theme/screenLayout.ts`:

- **Top:** `spacing.lg` between the title row and the first body control
- **Horizontal:** `spacing.lg` on both sides of that body

`MobileScreenContainer` already applies this. Home's feed list and Search's field / chips / list
must use the same helper — not a one-off `padding` / `margin`, and not a second inner `Card`
padding on top of the page gutter.

Screen lists (Home, Search, Library, …) are unboxed: no perimeter `Card` around the rows. `Card`
is a surface for grouped settings or section chrome, not for a scrolling result list.

Internal gaps stay on the screen. Prefer one column **`gap`** for a stack of related controls so
spaces stay equal by construction (Search: field → chips → list rule all share `spacing.base`).
**Spacing symmetry:** when two sides of a control should feel like the same relationship (above
and below chips, around a divider, between paired labels), use the same token — do not mix
`base` on one side and `md` on the other. Centered empty / loading (`VerticalCenter`,
`CallToActionSection`, `LoadingSection`) fills leftover height; it does not replace the page gutter.

## Search field and chips

Search uses **`SearchField`**: tertiary fill, no resting outline, leading magnifying-glass, a 2px
transparent border that becomes `tokens.border.primary` on focus. Do not restyle a bare
`TextInput` with a perimeter stroke.

Two or three filters under a field use **`OptionChipGroup`**. Selected chip = `buttonPrimary` fill.
Settings density (2–3 chips vs option-list screen) is **mobile-settings-option-density**.

## List rows

Media and result rows use **`HomeFeedRow`** (or **`ListRow`** when the layout is title/subtitle
only). Default vertical padding is **`tokens.spacing.base`**. Row artwork is **60×60**. Space
between title, subtitle, and other in-row lines with a column **`gap`** (`spacing.sm`) — not
`marginTop` / `marginBottom` on each line — so a missing subtitle or metadata line adds no leftover
space. The text stack uses `justifyContent: 'center'` so it stays vertically centered on the
artwork. The row itself uses `gap` between artwork and text (not a leading `marginLeft`).

Row dividers are `StyleSheet.hairlineWidth` + `themeStyles.border.borderColor`. The **last row
omits the bottom border** so a hairline does not sit on the list edge. Pass `isLast` on
`HomeFeedRow`. `ListSection` already supplies it as the third `renderItem` argument
`(item, index, isLast)`. `ReorderableSections` uses the same last-row rule.

The rule between chips/filters and the first row is one step stronger than a row hairline:
`height: 1`, the same `themeStyles.border.borderColor`, and horizontal inset from
`screenBodyInsets().paddingHorizontal` (Search's `listRule`). Do not invent a second color.

## Fill empty lists do not scroll

When a list's only body is a fill info state (`VerticalCenter` / `LoadingSection` /
`CallToActionSection` as `ListEmptyComponent`), there is nothing to scroll. Use **`FillList`**
instead of raw `FlatList` — it locks bounce, over-scroll, pull-to-refresh, and `scrollEnabled`
whenever `data` is empty and `ListEmptyComponent` is set. Pass `ListEmptyComponent={null}` when
the empty copy lives in the header and the list should still scroll (filter-no-matches).

## Action-gated account / membership

When the screen is usable and one control is gated, keep the control visible. On press, call
`useMembershipGate().openGate(reason)` so `ConfirmDialog` explains the denial. `needs_account`
confirms to Login; membership reasons confirm to the Membership screen. Do not park an inline
"Account required" card (`GatedFeatureNotice`) above a button the user has not tapped.

The exception is a **fill empty**: the whole body is missing because the feature requires an
account (Library history, playlists). That still uses **`CallToActionSection`** below.

Helper copy that is not the content itself (directory explainer, why-add notes) uses
**`HelperNote`** — tertiary fill and a leading info icon — so it does not read as a description.

## Login-gated fill states

When a screen's body is empty because the feature requires an account, use **`CallToActionSection`**
(it already wraps `VerticalCenter`) plus a Login action — not a bare `ListEmpty` and not
`authentication.login_required`. Prefer **`AuthAwareLoadState`** with `showAuthRequired` and a
feature-specific `authMessageKey` when the screen already uses that wrapper; otherwise wire
`CallToActionSection` as the `FillList` empty (or the only `MobileScreenContainer` child).

The message must explain **why the feature is worth logging in for** (what they get: synced inbox,
history across devices, playlists they can share). Generic “Log in to continue.” is for errors and
inline gates, not a full-screen feature empty. Hide the in-body heading on that fill — the
`HeaderBar` title is enough.

## Do not

- Use a different page gutter (`md`, `2xl`, raw numbers) for the body under `HeaderBar`.
- Rebuild the title-bar height or type in a screen-local `StyleSheet`.
- Add a divider, hairline, or shadow under `HeaderBar`.
- Put a second in-body display heading on a screen that already has a `HeaderBar` title.
- Use raw `FlatList` for a screen list that shows a `VerticalCenter` fill empty, then hand-toggle
  `scrollEnabled` / `bounces` at the screen.
- Leave a bottom hairline on the last list row, or drop media-row vertical padding back to
  `spacing.md`.

